# CH18 — Names for the Living. Veyr: the canals, the lower registry, Sak, Jori's satchel.

@scene CH18_JORI
if ch:CH18 after
say jori | You came through Bellharbor? Then you know I've been trying to reach Sak. He's under the square, in the lower registry.
say jori | Voss's remnants want the ledgers - the ones that prove what they did. Sak won't let them near. He won't let anyone near, including the people whose names are in there.
say jori | The canals changed when the walls fell. The ladder by the south of the square goes down; the lock gates raise the crossings.
objective dain | Reach the lower registry through Veyr's changed canals (ladder, south of the square).
end
label after
say jori | Go on. I'll bring the satchel when it's time.
@end

@scene CH18_GATE1
if flag:t02c_gate1 done
sfx FX010
set t02c_gate1
say narr | The west lock gate rises. Water drops in the west channel, and a crossing shoulders up out of it.
end
label done
say narr | The west crossing is up.
@end

@scene CH18_GATE2
if flag:t02c_gate2 done
sfx FX010
set t02c_gate2
say narr | The middle gate grinds open. The centre crossing surfaces, streaming.
end
label done
say narr | The middle crossing is up.
@end

@scene CH18_GATE3
if flag:t02c_gate3 done
sfx FX010
set t02c_gate3
say narr | The east gate lifts. The last crossing rises toward the registry stair.
end
label done
say narr | The east crossing is up.
@end

@scene CH18_REMNANTS once
say narr | Uniforms at the registry door, stripped of rank but not of habit. Voss's remnants.
say guard | The ledgers are ministry property. Stand aside.
say dain | The ministry sank. The names didn't.
battle D02P_2 noflee
set t02r_clear
say narr | The remnants scatter back into the canals. Behind a barricade of filing cabinets, someone coughs.
@end

@scene CH18_PIP
if ch:CH18 after
say pip | Don't - oh. Oh, it's you. It's actually you.
if party:C03 corren
goto cont
label corren
say pip | And Vespera! Alive! Nobody told me you could survive falling off a sky.
label cont
say pip | I've been guarding the originals. Every forged pass I ever made is in here, next to the real name it replaced.
say pip | If the remnants get these, they burn them. If the refugees get them, they - I don't know what they'll do. That's what scares me.
say oriel | That's not yours to decide, Sak.
say pip | I made the forgeries. Doesn't that make it mine to fix?
say dain | It makes it yours to answer for. Not to decide.
objective dain | Bring the original ledgers to the residents at the tables and let them choose how their names are recorded.
end
label after
say pip | New seal, blank forms, no forgeries. It's a very boring satchel now. I love it.
@end

@scene CH18_LEDGERS
if flag:t02r_names done
if !flag:t02r_clear blocked
say narr | The original ledgers, stacked on the tables. Sak hovers.
say survivor | This one's mine. Page forty. That's the name the ministry gave me when they sold my contract.
say elder | And here's the name my mother gave me. Different page.
say pip | I can write whichever you -
say survivor | No. We decide how it's written. You can hold the ink.
fade out 0.5
say narr | The residents take the ledgers one page at a time. Some keep the old names. Some write new ones. Each entry is signed by the person it belongs to.
fade in 0.5
set t02r_names
say jori | Sak.
say narr | Jori sets a worn leather satchel on the table - the one Sak used to carry false papers.
say jori | It's got blank forms in it now. And a proper seal, issued by the refugee assembly. It's yours, if you'll carry it.
say pip | ...I'm not forgiven.
say jori | No. You're employed.
say pip | That's better. That's so much better.
if party:C07 sableline
goto sabledone
label sableline
say sable | You and I signed the same kind of papers, Sak. Different hands. Same ink.
say pip | ...Then we both keep better ones now.
label sabledone
join C08
chapter CH18
objective dain | Sak is back. Veyr's distribution point is open.
call REUNION_CHECK
level_floor 29
end
label blocked
say narr | The ledgers are behind the barricade. Someone is guarding them.
end
label done
say narr | The ledgers, every entry signed by the person it names.
@end

@scene CH18_RES
if flag:t02r_names after
say survivor | We've been waiting for our own names. Not for someone to hand them to us.
end
label after
say survivor | Page forty. My name. My handwriting. Nobody else's.
@end

@scene T02R_REGISTRAR
if ch:CH20 q08
say clerk | Registry's open for amendments. Every change is signed by the one who asked for it.
end
label q08
call Q08_HOOK
@end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Veyr (post)
@scene T02P_ANSEL
if ch:CH20 q11
say ansel | Clerk Ansel. I refused false death certificates back when it could get me hanged. Now I sign ration chits. Better job.
end
label q11
call Q11_HOOK
@end

@scene T02P_GUARDS
say guard | Do you think our families can eat loyalty?
say soldier | Not anymore. They can eat the rations, though. So we hand out rations.
@end

@scene T02P_DIST
say worker | Distribution point. One line, no ranks. You'd be amazed how much faster it goes without ranks.
@end

@scene T02P_REFUGEE
say survivor | The throne used to be right there. Now it's a soup table. Nobody misses the throne.
@end

@scene T02P_SHOP
say keeper | South market, moved north because the south is underwater. Same prices. Mostly.
shop SHOP_T02
@end

@scene T02P_INN
say keeper | Barracks cots. Ex-barracks. Ex-cots, some of them, but they hold.
inn 0
@end
